-- THE HAMLETS HAVE THEIR FINDS (rome, 2026-11-04). The old village (Assart End,
-- once the Dens) has 27 things on its floors; its two copies had none. Each gets the same kind of find, only
-- where that room's own words carry it (the reason is beside each row). All
-- regrow, as the Dens' do. A live world lays each down once (zone.ts).


-- THE GEAR WAS CHEAP (rome, 2026-11-04): each hamlet gets a set like the old
-- village's from its own region's floor gear, commons and a few uncommons, and
-- the old village, all commons on ground surrounded by better, three of the
-- wood's uncommons. Never in a chapel: everything there was carried out.
